.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-CREATE-USER-GROUP 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-create-user-group \- create a new Euclid user group
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eam create-user-group
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I NAME
[\fB\-\-description\fR|\fB\-d\fR \fIDESCRIPTION\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a new, empty user group via the eam service's
.I create-user-group
action. The caller must be authenticated as an administrator (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1)).
.PP
A group starts out with no members - add users to it with
.BR euclid-cli-eam-user-group-add-user (1).
.PP
Group membership is also how administrator status works: a user is an
administrator if and only if it is a member of the group named
.IR administrator .
There is no per-user "is admin" flag; grant or revoke administrator
privileges by adding or removing a user from that group.
.PP
The created group's JSON representation is printed to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Group name, unique across the deployment. Required.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-description " " \fIDESCRIPTION\fR
Free-text description of the group's purpose. Defaults to an empty string.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The group was created.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the request could not be sent, the caller is
not an authenticated administrator, or a group with that name already
exists. If the failure was an expired or invalid session (\fIHTTP 401\fR),
the stored credentials file is removed; run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create an ordinary group:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam create-user-group \e
    --name developers --description "Application developers"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create the special \fIadministrator\fR group (if it doesn't already exist)
and add a user to it:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam create-user-group \e
    --name administrator --description "Euclid administrators"

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam user-group-add-user \e
    --user-group ern:euclid:eam:eu-central-1:000000000000:userGroup:administrator \e
    --user ern:euclid:eam:eu-central-1:000000000000:user:jdoe
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
